        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Hiwassee, North Carolina; Cherokee County, North Carolina; Swain County, North Carolina; Graham County, North Carolina; New York City\n- Dams: Hiwassee Dam; Fontana Dam\n- Water bodies: Hiwassee Reservoir; Hiwassee River; Little Tennessee River\n- Organizations/Systems: TVA system\n- People: Billy Bland\n- Topics: dam height rankings; hydroelectric dams; American R&B music\n\nFacts:\n- Fontana Dam is a hydroelectric dam on the Little Tennessee River in Swain and Graham counties, North Carolina, United States.\n- Billy Bland was born on 5 April 1932 in Wilmington, North Carolina.\n- Hiwassee Dam is 307 feet high and is the third highest dam in the TVA system, behind Fontana Dam and Watauga.\n- Hiwassee is a small village in Cherokee County, North Carolina, next to Hiwassee Dam and the artificially created Hiwassee Reservoir on the Hiwassee River.\n- Billy Bland was an American R&B singer and songwriter.\n- Billy Bland died on 22 March 2017 in New York City.",
